\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Planned six-link routing architecture for miniLISA. Each spacecraft has an optical source and an independently referenced Moku phasemeter that also supplies its EOM drive; each delay-line board can synthesize two incoming links. The complete routing supports six directed links, whereas the Michelson calculation in Section~\ref {sec:performance} uses links $12$, $21$, $13$ and $31$. The spacecraft-1 and reference lasers are stabilized to separate optical cavities; the other spacecraft lasers are phase-locked to synthesized beat notes. The common reference laser supplies the optical heterodyne reference.}}{7}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:triangular}{{2}{7}{Planned six-link routing architecture for miniLISA. Each spacecraft has an optical source and an independently referenced Moku phasemeter that also supplies its EOM drive; each delay-line board can synthesize two incoming links. The complete routing supports six directed links, whereas the Michelson calculation in Section~\ref {sec:performance} uses links $12$, $21$, $13$ and $31$. The spacecraft-1 and reference lasers are stabilized to separate optical cavities; the other spacecraft lasers are phase-locked to synthesized beat notes. The common reference laser supplies the optical heterodyne reference}{figure.2}{}}
